<title>JAPAN: Yaohan shares remain weaker in morning.</title>
<headline>Yaohan shares remain weaker in morning.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yaohan Japan Corp, a medium-sized supermarket chain operator, remained weaker on Monday morning, prompted by the news on Friday that Japan Securities Finance Co Ltd (JSF) had announced it would stop accepting orders to borrow Yaohan shares for margin transactions, traders said.</p>
<p>Yaohan shares briefly dropped to 186 yen, a new low for this calendar year. At 0139 GMT, they were off 15 yen at 188. Volume was 1.031 million shares.</p>
</text>
